{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791634999,"nonce":"gCQuY1RULMS6fXaMRonGwgh7fGM=","title":"cn navigation menu rebuilds its whole bar on hover, and its labels can wrap","message":"The bar was a Stateful whose deps were the open-menu signal, so opening or switching a menu rebuilt every item. Each link and trigger was a further Stateful\u003cButtonState\u003e whose on_state took no state, kept for hover, and a trigger's \"active\" look was captured when the bar was built, which is why the whole bar had to rebuild. reset_button_state cleared hover stuck on the other triggers' FSMs.\n\nLabels were wrapping text, so a label whose box came out narrower than its glyphs folded (\"Hom\" / \"e\" in cn_demo; the box size itself is b43626b).\n\nFix: one plain Div bar. An item's hover is an Interaction; a trigger carries `cn-nav-link--active` through class_when over the open-menu signal, so the theme's existing `.cn-nav-link--active` rule paints it; the label and chevron colour is a computed over both. Labels are no_wrap and items flex_shrink_0, as shadcn's `w-max` trigger. NavigationLink, a Stateful only for the hover the stylesheet already gives it, is a plain Div.\n\nTests: `blinc_cn/tests/navigation_menu_in_place.rs`: hovering a trigger opens its menu and marks only it active, hovering a link brightens it and leaving restores it, with every pointer move checked for subtree rebuilds; labels cannot wrap. All three fail against the old component.","files":null}]}